
Suppose we are facing a binary classification learning problem with the feature space $\Xspace = \{0,1\}$ and label space $\Yspace=\{-1,1\}$.
%	
Let us assume that the relationship between the feature $X$ and the label $Y$ is specified by
%
$$ Y = 2 \max\{X, \epsilon\} - 1 $$
%	
where $\P_X = \mathrm{Ber}(\theta_X)$, $\P_\epsilon = \mathrm{Ber}(\theta_\epsilon)$, and $X$ and $\epsilon$ are independent.
% 
%	
\begin{enumerate}	  
  \item 

    What is $H(\epsilon)$? 

  \item
    What is $H(Y|X)$? 

  \item 
    What is $H(Y,X)$? 

  \item
    Now assume instead that $\epsilon = \psi(X)$ for some deterministic function $\psi: \{0,1\} \to \{0,1\}$,
    so $X$ and $\epsilon$ are in general no longer independent.
    What are the answers to the previous questions in this case? 

\end{enumerate}